  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Masha put a multiplication sign between the second and third digits of the number 2020 and noted that the resulting product $20\\times20$ was a square number. How many integers between 2010 and 2099 (including 2020) have the same property?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "1"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "2"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "3"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "4"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "5"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Make 20 times the number square",
    "body": "The numbers are $20ab$ and the product is $20\\times ab$ where $ab$ is a two-digit number from 10 to 99. Since $20=2^2\\times5$, the product is a square exactly when $ab=5k^2$ for some integer $k$. In the range 10 to 99: $5\\times4=20$, $5\\times9=45$, $5\\times16=80$ (and $5\\times1=5$, $5\\times25=125$ are out of range).\n\nSo the numbers are 2020, 2045 and 2080: three of them.\n\n**Answer: (C) 3**"
   }
  ],
