  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Divisibility by 18",
    "body": "A number is divisible by 18 when it is divisible by 2 and by 9. The digit sum is $1+2+\\dots+9=45$, so every arrangement is divisible by 9. So the number is divisible by 18 exactly when it is even, i.e. its last digit is 2, 4, 6 or 8. By symmetry each digit is equally likely to be last, so the probability is $\\frac49$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac49$**"
   }
