  "blankPoints": null,
  "wrongPoints": null,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Kanga labelled the vertices of a square-based pyramid using 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 once each. For each face Kanga calculated the sum of the numbers on its vertices. Four of these sums equalled 7, 8, 9 and 10. What is the sum for the fifth face?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "11"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "12"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "13"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "14"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "15"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Find the apex label",
    "body": "Let $x$ be the label at the apex. The square face has the other four labels, so its sum is $15-x\\ge10$. If the square were one of the four given sums, it would be 10 and $x=5$. Then the face with sum 7 would be a triangle face containing the apex 5, but such a face has sum at least $5+1+2=8$, a contradiction. So the square is not among the given faces, and the four triangular faces have sums $7,8,9,10$, total 34.\n\nEach triangular face contains the apex, and each base vertex lies in exactly two triangular faces. So the four triangle sums add to $4x+2(15-x)=2x+30$. Hence $2x+30=34$, $x=2$, and the square face has sum $15-2=13$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 13**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "algebra",
   "logic"
  ],
  "difficulty": 3,
